    schema:description "Clariness is looking for an Affiliate & Partnerships Manager (f/m/d) based in Berlin, Hamburg, Cape Town, UK, or Serbia. - Full-time; unlimited - About the role: As an Affiliate & Partnerships Manager, you will play a key role in expanding and managing our network of affiliate partners and strategic relationships to support patient recruitment across global clinical trials. Working closely with Marketing, Patient Recruitment, Clinical Operations, and external partners, you will identify new growth opportunities, optimize partner performance, and help drive high-quality patient acquisition. This role is ideal for someone who combines strong relationship-building skills with a data-driven approach to performance marketing and partnership management. Tasks As an Affiliate & Partnerships Manager, you would be responsible for: Developing, managing, and growing affiliate and strategic partner relationships to support patient recruitment initiatives. Identifying, onboarding, and maintaining relationships with affiliates, publishers, patient advocacy groups, and other strategic partners. Coordinating partner campaigns and optimizing partner performance to maximize recruitment outcomes. Collaborating with Marketing teams to support performance marketing initiatives and improve acquisition across digital channels. Monitoring affiliate and campaign performance using key metrics and providing recommendations to improve lead quality, conversion, and ROI. Ensuring affiliate and partnership activities comply with applicable healthcare, privacy, and marketing regulations. Working closely with Marketing, Patient Recruitment, Clinical Operations, Compliance, Analytics, and external partners to identify new opportunities and continuously improve recruitment performance. Requirements We would like you to have: Bachelor's degree in Marketing, Business, Communications, Healthcare Administration, or a related field. 5+ years of experience in affiliate marketing, partnership management, business development, digital marketing, or a similar role. Proven experience developing and managing affiliate programs, strategic partnerships, or publisher relationships. Strong understanding of performance marketing principles, including CPA, CPL, CPC, attribution, and campaign optimization. Experience supporting digital marketing campaigns across channels such as Google Ads, Meta Ads, display advertising, or other paid media platforms. Strong analytical skills with experience using reporting dashboards, web analytics, and campaign performance metrics to drive data-informed decisions. Fluency in English with proven experience in the U.S. digital environment, including knowledge of U.S. consumer behavior, advertising platforms, campaign practices, and market-specific regulations. Experience working in healthcare, life sciences, clinical research, or another regulated industry is a strong advantage. Excellent communication, negotiation, stakeholder management, and relationship-building skills. Benefits You may ask now, why should I work for you? Let us give you a few reasons – and you'll learn more during the process. A varied and exciting job with a lot of personal responsibility in an international company, where you can develop and expand your skills. Professional and personal development opportunities - incl. personal development budget. Flexible working hours and mobile working. Regular team events and open feedback culture. A versatile field of activity and challenging projects. A supportive and open company culture, providing the opportunity to collaborate with a diverse and professional team. Impact healthcare by accelerating medical innovation through improved access to clinical trials, potentially bringing needed treatments to patients faster. How to apply & what to expect: Apply via link (CV only; no cover letter required). Introductory call (30 min) → Technical interview → Senior Leadership Interview → Take Home Test → Demo Day → Decision. We aim to move promptly and keep you updated at every step. At Clariness, we are proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees, regardless of race, religion, gender, sexual orientation, national origin, disability or age. Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
