<https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/live/job/arbeitnow-infrastructure-platform-engineer-london-230029> a prov:Entity,
        schema:JobPosting ;
    dcterms:source <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/source/arbeitnow> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-25T22:33:23+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/bluecrestcapitalmanagement/infrastructure-platform-engineer-london-230029> ;
    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "059336bfe13c2753a01d48f76f84df7bbb2809f1a11393ae3de1188e781eacff" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-08-25T14:52:28+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-08-25T22:33:23+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "infrastructure-platform-engineer-london-230029" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "<p><strong>Department Overview:</strong></p> <p>Our Technology Infrastructure team operates globally and is responsible for every aspect of the firm's hybrid platform. This ranges from our EUC/Office environments to Trading and Core service Co-Location Data Centres, and extends to Public Cloud, delivering top-tier technology services to a dynamic and demanding Trading organisation.<br><br>In addition to meeting the round-the-clock operational demands of the platforms, we continuously evolve and transform our platforms to maintain a competitive edge that our business requires. We innovate to provide valuable solutions and leverage our skilled Technology teams to deliver against rapidly changing business requirements.</p> <p><strong>Role Overview:&nbsp;</strong></p> <p>The Platform Engineer, Network Services focus will be responsible for managing, supporting, and enhancing BlueCrest’s global network infrastructure, including data networks, telecommunications, network security, advanced IP services, and unified communications.</p> <p>This role sits within the Infrastructure Platform team and offers opportunities to work across other core platforms, including Linux, Storage, Windows and Hypervisors. As a result, a broad range of experience and a strong understanding of how wider technology infrastructure platforms integrate and co-exist would be beneficial. In particular, solid Unix operating system knowledge and operational experience would be an advantage.</p> <p>Additionally, we are looking for engineers who bring the experience and mindset needed to help us adopt modern technology practices, including Infrastructure as Code, AI-enabled operations, automation-led delivery, and SRE practices. As we continue to grow our hybrid networking capabilities across on-premise/colocation, Azure and AWS, we are seeking expertise in designing, building, and supporting robust, deterministic cloud network environments.</p> <p><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p> <ul> <li>Monitor, support, and maintain BlueCrest’s global networks and related systems.</li> <li>Carry out BAU changes across all network systems in line with the change control process.</li> <li>Design and build network products for on-premises data centres, colocation trading, offices, WAN, and cloud infrastructure.</li> <li>Responsible for network security area, with experience operating and maintaining next-generation firewall platforms.</li> <li>Develop and maintain network systems and associated code, following Infrastructure as Code and SRE practices.</li> <li>Design and deliver project work across all networking disciplines and wider infrastructure platforms.</li> <li>Contribute to the architecture and roadmap for BlueCrest’s networks and platforms.</li> <li>Maintain data centre and communications room environments, including racking and patching network equipment.</li> <li>Manage third-party vendors, data centre providers, and telecoms providers.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Experience and Skills required:&nbsp;</strong></p> <p>An experienced network engineer with a minimum of 5 years of experience working in a financial institution/ fast-paced environment</p> <p><strong>Essential Skills</strong></p> <ul> <li>Deep understanding of TCP/IP protocols and networking fundamentals, equivalent to CCNP level.</li> <li>Strong Cisco hardware, switching, and routing experience across data centre and enterprise networks.</li> <li>Cisco ACI</li> <li>Cisco IOS-XE switches and routers <ul> <li>Cisco ACI</li> <li>Cisco IOS-XE switches and routers</li> </ul> </li> <li>Experience with next-generation firewalls, particularly Palo Alto platforms.</li> <li>BAU changes: Policies, NAT, Routing</li> <li>Monitoring: analyse firewall logs with next gen features <ul> <li>BAU changes: Policies, NAT, Routing</li> <li>Monitoring: analyse firewall logs using next-generation firewall features.</li> </ul> </li> <li>Proficient with fundamental Unix operating system knowledge, skills, and working experience.</li> <li>Advanced Azure and AWS cloud networking experience.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Desirable Skills</strong></p> <ul> <li>Infrastructure as Code and SRE for Network skills including using API, Programming, Scripting and Orchestration skills <ul> <li>Python, Ansible and Terraform</li> <li>Rest APIs</li> <li>CI/CD pipeline</li> </ul> </li> <li>Experience in office infrastructure design, build and migration.</li> <li>Experience in Datacentre physical and logical migrations.</li> <li>Network performance monitoring and packet capture.</li> <li>Experience in support VoIP technologies. <ul> <li>Avaya Enterprise Call Managers or equivalent</li> <li>Turret system or equivalent trade voice</li> <li>Microsoft Teams</li> </ul> </li> </ul> <p><strong>About You:</strong></p> <p>The ideal candidate will be joining a progressive and collaborative working environment that promotes teamwork, technical excellence, and innovative solutions.&nbsp;This role is particularly suitable for a team player who is highly motivated and thrives in a dynamic, fast-paced and demanding trading environment.&nbsp;We are seeking someone who can work autonomously, efficiently and methodically under pressure, multi-tasking and adapting quickly to learn new skills.&nbsp;An experienced platform engineer with networks focus and a minimum of 5 years of experience working in a financial institution or within a fast-paced dynamic environment would be a suitable fit for this role.&nbsp;This role may require flexible working hours to implement changes out of business hours in all regions (US/EMEA/APAC) and respond to P1 issue callout.&nbsp;The selected candidate will have access to the latest technology, opportunities to grow professionally and technically, as well as supporting training resources available to them.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><em>BlueCrest is committed to providing an inclusive environment for its workforce. As an employer, we provide equal opportunities to all people regardless of their gender, marital or civil partnership status, race, religion or ethnicity, disability, age, sexual orientation or nationality. </em></p> Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-bluecrestcapitalmanagement ;
    schema:identifier "arbeitnow-infrastructure-platform-engineer-london-230029" ;
    schema:jobLocation [ a schema:Place ;
            schema:name "London" ] ;
    schema:title "Infrastructure Platform Engineer" ;
    schema:url <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/bluecrestcapitalmanagement/infrastructure-platform-engineer-london-230029> .

<https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/live/job/arbeitnow-interim-fpa-director-6-months-ftc-238082> a prov:Entity,
        schema:JobPosting ;
    dcterms:source <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/source/arbeitnow> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-25T22:33:23+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/everway/interim-fpa-director-6-months-ftc-238082> ;
    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "b36fbb47587ae0a40c0dfdd9abf4ba633a44036c6de886548303e80585016c6b" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-08-25T06:56:47+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-08-25T22:33:23+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "interim-fpa-director-6-months-ftc-238082" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "<div class=\"content-intro\"><p>Every mind is unique. Yet much of the world is still built for what’s considered \"normal,\" leaving too many people behind. At Everway, we change that by creating technology that helps everyone understand and be understood. By understanding and addressing the unique needs of each individual, we're creating a world where differences are recognized and valued.</p> <p>Our careers fit real life. When you join us, you’re not just taking a job. You’re joining a movement to build a more neuroinclusive world. We’re a global community of over 800 employees spanning North America, UK, Europe, Australia, and New Zealand. A career here is purposeful and fast-moving, with clear expectations, modern tools, and the clarity to focus on what matters most.&nbsp;</p> <p>Our people are supported and encouraged to show up as they are, with different ways of thinking welcomed and valued. We pride ourselves on our core values that are embedded within our culture. These are to <strong>be curious, have courage, and commit fully</strong>.</p> <p>Join us at Everway - together, we can unlock the full potential of every mind.</p></div><p><strong>About the role</strong></p> <p>The Interim FP&amp;A Director will provide senior support across corporate planning and executive reporting during a critical period for the Finance function. You'll work closely with the SVP, Strategic Finance and VP, Corporate FP&amp;A, with a particular focus on Board reporting, strategic analysis and the company's three-year plan.</p> <p>This is a hands-on interim assignment combining detailed financial modelling and planning with senior stakeholder communication. You'll help translate business performance and forecasts into a clear, credible narrative and maintain the quality and continuity of key Strategic Finance deliverables.</p> <p><em><strong>This is a six-month fixed-term contract role.</strong></em></p> <h2><strong>Main responsibilities</strong></h2> <p>In this role, you will:</p> <ul> <li>Own the preparation and coordination of Board and executive reporting materials, including financial analysis, commentary and final review, ensuring key messages, risks and actions are clear.</li> <li>Support the development of the company's three-year plan, including the narrative connecting strategic priorities with financial outcomes.</li> <li>Build and refine scenario analysis, sensitivities and planning assumptions across revenue, costs, headcount and cash flow.</li> <li>Partner with Finance and business leaders to align assumptions and strengthen the overall planning process.</li> <li>Provide senior day-to-day support to the SVP Strategic Finance, working with the VP of Corporate FP&amp;A and other Strategic Finance VPs across planning, reporting and ad hoc strategic analysis as required.</li> <li>Identify practical improvements to reporting cadence, KPI definition, forecasting discipline and FP&amp;A processes.</li> </ul> <h2><strong>Essential criteria</strong></h2> <ul> <li>3–5+ years of relevant professional experience at a similar level across corporate finance, strategic finance, strategy or management consulting, or FP&amp;A.</li> <li>Experience producing Board packs, executive presentations and decision-support materials for senior stakeholders.</li> <li>Experience supporting long-range planning, budgeting, forecasting and strategic financial modelling.</li> <li>Advanced Excel and financial modelling capability, with experience producing accurate, high-quality planning and reporting outputs.</li> <li>Experience working closely with CFO-level or other senior stakeholders and constructively challenging assumptions.</li> </ul> <h2><strong>Desirable criteria</strong></h2> <ul> <li>Experience in SaaS, technology, PE-backed or similarly dynamic business environments.</li> <li>Experience integrating AI into finance or FP&amp;A working practices.</li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Please submit your application by <strong>Monday 7th September 2026.</strong></p> <p>Please note: applications may close early due to high demand, so early submission is encouraged.</p><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p>Join our team and enjoy a competitive salary with bonus opportunities, flexible work schedules, and comprehensive health and wellness benefits. We offer flexible time off plans, career growth through development programs, and a collaborative, innovative culture where your ideas matter.&nbsp; Ready to make an impact? Apply today and be part of a company that invests in your success!</p> <p>We are committed to providing a Drug-Free Workplace for all employees.</p> <p>We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law.</p> <p>You can view our Recruitment and Selection Policy <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yDxHyVbhh8MK9NnCYdnEAfVSO4rhPCovVbKK8ecxT4U/edit?usp=sharing\">here.</a></p> <p>Please click the link for our <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uAKvHVSRsqZ83CGhM3_3Dc6RPsXwlTdmwdUH7msHkVM/edit?usp=sharing\">Privacy Notice</a></p> <p>&nbsp;</p></div> Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-everway ;
