    schema:datePosted "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Join the dynamic team at Bank of Communications Frankfurt Branch as a Specialist in Regulatory Reporting and Taxation. Established in 2007, our branch serves as a vital link between China and Europe, contributing to global trade and financial operations. As part of one of China's leading banks with over 2,900 branches worldwide, you'll work within a diverse team of around 40 Chinese and German professionals. Our Frankfurt branch is known for its comprehensive financial services, including national and international payment processing, overseas trading, lending, deposit banking, and more. In this role, you'll collaborate with our seven specialized departments to ensure compliance with regulatory requirements and optimize taxation processes. Your expertise will support our mission to facilitate seamless financial interactions across borders, making a significant impact on our operations. We value innovation, precision, and teamwork, offering a challenging yet rewarding environment for growth and professional development. Tasks Option A – Regulatory Reporting Prepare and submit regulatory and statistical reports in accordance with German and European banking regulations including reports tot eh relevant deposit protection scheme. Ensure reporting accuracy and compliance with regulatory deadlines. Validate and reconcile financial data between banking systems and regulatory reporting systems. Monitor developments in CRR, CRD VI and other regulatory requirements and advise the senior management in this regard. Support implementation of new regulatory reporting requirements. Cooperate with the IT team to maintain the requisite reporting systems and access to reporting platforms from relevant supervisory authorities. Respond to external and internal audit requests related to regulatory matters. Liaise with supervisory authorities and external service providers where required. Option B –Taxation Preparation of annual accounts under German GAAP Prepare tax calculations, tax returns and tax filings under German tax law. Support corporate tax, trade tax and VAT compliance. Monitor withholding tax obligations relating to cross-border transactions. Support transfer pricing documentation. Assist with implementation of OECD Pillar Two and other present and upcoming, national and international requirements. Coordinate tax audits and communicate with tax authorities and external tax advisers. Respond to external and internal audit requests related to accounting and tax matters. Requirements Candidates are expected to possess the following qualifications and skills: A university degree in Finance, Accounting, Taxation, Economics, or a related field, or an equivalent certification. A professional accounting or tax qualification is considered advantageous. Relevant professional experience in banking, finance, or auditing sectors. For Regulatory Reporting: A strong understanding of CRR, CRD, KWG, and regulatory reporting requirements. For German Taxation: Comprehensive knowledge of German corporate taxation and international taxation principles. Strong analytical capabilities with a keen attention to detail. Proficiency in MS Office applications. Excellent command of the English language. Proficiency in German. Benefits We offer: Employment in a small, flexible team with the opportunity to gain comprehensive insights into all aspects of banking. Independent and diverse responsibilities within an international bank featuring streamlined communication channels. Performance-based compensation along with standard banking benefits such as transportation subsidies and meal vouchers. A modern workplace environment located in Frankfurt's banking district, complete with a cafeteria. Post-work activities including various hobby groups and access to an in-house fitness center. Opportunities for intercultural exchange within a collegial and familial atmosphere. 30 days of annual leave with two additional days off on December 24th and 31st. A break room offering panoramic views of Frankfurt's skyline, providing a space to relax and enjoy coffee. Join Bank of Communications Frankfurt Branch as a Specialist in Regulatory Reporting/Taxation. Enhance your career in a dynamic, international banking environment. Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
